Abstract
One of the major challenges we face these days while we travel somewhere is to find a parking spot. This is due to the rapid increase in the usage of vehicles (four-wheeler specifically). We often lose our patience while searching for the right place to park our vehicle, some end up parking on the side of the road which results in traffic jams. During peak hours you can’t even think of travelling unless you already have a dedicated parking spot at the place where you are heading to, which is rare. Even at the places with commercial parking area, it is a hustling task to search for a vacant place this leads to more consumption of fuel and hence contributing to increase pollution rates. This paper aims at resolving the problem by designing an automated parking system. To account for the same, we need to design a Web application, using which a person can pre book a slot in the nearest parking area (hassle-free). It will also navigate the user to the booked slot. Also, the area would be embedded with certain components for monitoring purpose to ensure smooth running of the automated system. Payments can be carried out digitally with ease thanks to services like Google Pay, Paytm, PhonePe and debit/credit card. This will reduce human interaction, traffic jams and no more delay to attend important morning meetings. All the results and algorithm in this paper are developed using HTML, CSS, Bootstrap framework(back-end). (Front-end) 
Keywords— Automated parking system; Web application; monitoring components; digital payment; smart allocation of slots; reducing pollution
